Speech Script (5-Minute Pitch)
[Slide 1: Title Slide] (0:00 - 0:35)
"Hello everyone, and thank you for being here. I’m proud to introduce OurHome—a platform where data-driven technology meets profound human empathy. At its core,
OurHome is engineered to redefine how we support individuals navigating Major Depressive Disorder, Generalized Anxiety, and ADHD. We are building this with two 
clear global missions in mind: SDG 3 (Good Health and Well-being) and SDG 10 (Reduced Inequalities), by democratizing a highly sophisticated, yet completely 
pressure-free mental health tool."

[Slide 2: The Philosophy & SDGs] (0:35 - 1:25)
"To understand OurHome, we have to look at the sociology of 'Affective Presencing' and 'Co-Mobility.' Research shows that for someone experiencing executive 
dysfunction, standard 'active' care is actually harmful. When a loved one texts, 'Did you eat?' or 'How are you?', it demands a cognitive response. It induces 
guilt, pressure, and ultimately, withdrawal.
The solution is Passive Co-Presence. In physical psychology, this is called 'Body Doubling'—sharing a room in silence to create motivation and safety. Our 
mission was to figure out how to digitize that exact psychological safety net across distances."

[Slide 3: Structured Interaction Data] (1:25 - 2:15)
"We achieved this by building a sophisticated data engine. OurHome doesn't ask the user how they feel; it learns it. We capture highly structured time-series 
metrics.
First, Routine Kinetics: We log the exact timestamps of micro-habit completions, like hydration or making the bed.
Second, Ambient Engagement: We track the duration and frequency of silent profile views. When someone just opens the app to look at their partner's routine—that
is virtual body doubling.
Third, Micro-Cue Telemetry: We analyze non-verbal interactions, like the exact moment a user triggers a virtual 'Send Hug' signal. This gives us a rich, 
tabular dataset of human behavior."

[Slide 4: Machine Learning Implementation] (2:15 - 3:15)
"This dataset is the lifeblood of our Machine Learning architecture. Because we are dealing with structured time-series data rather than images or audio, we 
don't need heavy deep learning. We apply highly interpretable algorithms like Random Forest and XGBoost.
What does the AI actually do?

Anomaly & Energy Detection: The model infers depressive or high-anxiety phases by recognizing temporal shifts—like a sudden drop in ambient engagement or 
delayed habit logging.

Adaptive UI Scaling: When the algorithm detects high cognitive load, it dynamically simplifies the user interface. It hides complex tasks and surfaces only 
the most vital, basic micro-steps to prevent overwhelming the user.

Algorithmic Nudging: The model predicts the optimal emotional window for a caregiver to send a silent support cue, ensuring connection happens when it is 
needed most."

[Slide 5: The Human Interface] (3:15 - 4:05)
"All of this complex data processing results in a beautifully simple, Zero-Expectation UI. The interface is divided into Personal and Shared spaces.
Because mental fatigue makes typing and decision-making difficult, everything operates on 1-click presets. The user doesn't write tasks; they simply tap 
pre-populated micro-steps. Everything syncs in real-time via Firebase, providing immediate, silent visual feedback. I check a box; my partner sees it miles 
away. We are connected, without saying a word."

[Slide 6: Ethical & Clinical Boundaries] (4:05 - 5:00)
"Finally, because we are dealing with behavioral data, our ethical boundaries are absolute. Our data pipeline is GDPR and HIPAA compliant, utilizing strict 
anonymization with zero Personally Identifiable Information.
Furthermore, we intentionally avoid diagnostic labels. OurHome is a supportive companion, not a clinical judge. We are using machine learning not to demand 
productivity, but to remove pressure.
Technology is at its best when it adapts to human vulnerability. That is what OurHome does. Thank you for your time."
